-- title:
--   Orthogonal of the toric lattice in Tₚ J_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 1$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^2\nmid M$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and $M/p\neq 0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data at $p$ for $(M,H)$ — a structure morphism $\sigma_A$, a scheme $X$ with a morphism $f$ to the base, a relative group law, and bijections $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$, $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from $J_H(M/p)$ (for the image subgroup `infSubgroup`) and from $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the reduced function field onto sections of $f$ over the generic resp. residual point — and let $O$ be a Néron object for $J_H(M)$ over this data; $\Lambda.f$ is assumed smooth and proper with connected fibres and a relative group law, and $\Lambda.\mathrm{pts}$, $\Lambda.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ additive. Let $T_t$ be the $\mathbb Z_p$-submodule of $T=T_p J_H(M)$ consisting of the $x$ all of whose components $x_n$ lie in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^n)$ (the subgroup generated by the toric points of order $p^n$), assumed stable under the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting through `JH.tateGaloisRep`. Let $\alpha_H,\beta_H$ be integral, finite $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra maps from the function field of $X_{H'}(M/p)$ to that of $X_H(M)$ acting on $q$-expansions by the identity and by $q\mapsto q^p$; assume the two maps $O.\mathrm{degPts}\,0,\ O.\mathrm{degPts}\,1$ are computed by divisor push-forward along $\alpha_H$, $\beta_H$, and that the two homomorphisms $\alpha_{\mathrm{pull}}\,0,\ \alpha_{\mathrm{pull}}\,1 : J_{H'}(M/p)\to J_H(M)$ are computed by divisor pull-back along $\alpha_H$, $\beta_H$. Let $T_{\mathrm{old}}\le T$ consist of the $x$ for which there are $w_0,w_1\in T_pJ_{H'}(M/p)$ with $x_n=\alpha_{\mathrm{pull}}0(w_{0,n})+\alpha_{\mathrm{pull}}1(w_{1,n})$ for all $n$. Assume further: for some $k$, $p^k\cdot(\tau x-x)\in T_{\mathrm{old}}\sqcup T_t$ for all $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup at $A$ and all $x\in T$; any $o\in T_{\mathrm{old}}$ with $O.\mathrm{degPts}\,j$ vanishing on every component is zero; there are homomorphisms $J_H(M)\to J_1(M)\to J_H(M)$ whose composite is multiplication by some $c>0$; and there are a compatible system $\zeta_n$ of primitive $p^n$-th roots of unity with $\zeta_{n+1}^p=\zeta_n$ and a $\mathbb Z_p$-bilinear form $e$ on $T$ which is levelwise given by divisorial Weil pairing data of order $p^n$ read through $\zeta_n$, skew-symmetric, and non-degenerate. Then there exists a single $k\in\mathbb N$ such that every $x\in T$ with $e(x,y)=0$ for all $y\in T_t$ satisfies $p^k\cdot x\in T_t\sqcup T_{\mathrm{old}}$.
--
--   This is the lattice form of Grothendieck's orthogonality theorem for the monodromy filtration at a prime of multiplicative reduction: the Weil orthogonal of the toric part is, up to a bounded power of $p$, the sum of the toric and the $p$-old parts of the Tate module of $J_H(M)$ at $p\parallel M$. It is the $J_H$-level engine for the corresponding statement on the diamond-fixed part of $T_pJ_1(M)$, which enters the level-lowering step at $p$.
